  "notes": "Sprint 156 T-005 — Auditor Baseline Collection Fix. Added 3-tag CiBaselineInvocationStatus (OK | SPAWN_FAIL | PARSE_FAIL) plus retry-once-on-spawn-fail logic to a new auditor-side helper `gatherCiBaseline`. Helper distinguishes (a) subprocess that never produced an exit code from (b) subprocess that ran but output was unparseable — both surface as zeroed counts so they cannot be mistaken for genuine regressions (Sprint 155 root cause). `parseVitestBaselineOutput` is a pure function covering JSON reporter shape AND the 'Tests X passed (Y)' footer with internal-consistency guard against the Sprint 155 phantom-fail pattern. `writeCiBaselineRecord` persists `.deckent/ci-baseline.json` with the new `vitest_invocation_status` field. Test scope: 16 new tests in tests/monitor/auditor-baseline.test.ts cover JSON-path parse, text-path parse, garbled-output PARSE_FAIL, JSON-internal-inconsistency rejection, spawn-fail-twice → SPAWN_FAIL, spawn-fail-once → retry success → OK, ENOENT error pattern, retry-disabled path, stderr tail truncation (2KB), record persistence for each status (OK/SPAWN_FAIL/PARSE_FAIL), .deckent dir auto-creation, and custom spawnFn injection. ANCHOR compliance: NO project-wide `npm run build` / `tsc --noEmit` over project / `vitest run` over project — `tsc --noEmit` invoked once as worker self-verify per WORKER-GUIDE (clean exit), and only `npx vitest run tests/monitor/auditor-baseline.test.ts` (16 pass) + `npx vitest run tests/monitor/` for monitor-suite regression (290/290 pass) were run. SCOPE: stayed strictly inside src/monitor/auditor.ts (append-only at file tail) + tests/monitor/auditor-baseline.test.ts (new file). ADR-003 (vitest) + ADR-006 (array args, no shell:true concat) + ADR-019 (subprocess discipline) honored. Migration path: src/core/plugin-hooks.ts:runPreSprintValidation can replace its current `runFullVitest`+`writeCiBaseline` pair with `gatherCiBaseline`+`writeCiBaselineRecord` in a follow-up task that owns the plugin-hooks.ts scope; that work is intentionally out of this task's scope. The new exports are immediately consumable by Brain pre-sprint hooks and the sprint reporter.",
